    "Because |d(log10 T_{1/2})/dQ_alpha| is ~3 to 8.5 dex/MeV across heavy alpha emitters, sub-dex half-life accuracy from internally predicted Q_alpha^{QOU} requires ~0.05 MeV relative mass-difference precision (~30 ppm of total B); smooth macroscopic FCC+TL / q-CLT binding laws without exact shell-closure terms miss Q_alpha by several MeV and shift log10 T_{1/2} by many dex."
